# InvestPal ecosystem credentials.
#
# `make setup` writes .env.secrets from this template at mode 600. Nothing here
# is required — the Claude Code cockpit works with every value blank.
#
# The Claude Code agent is denied read access to .env.secrets by the
# permissions.deny rules in .claude/settings.json. Keep credentials in this
# file rather than in .env, which the agent may read.
#
# Nothing here is ever exported into Claude Code's own process environment.
# scripts/lib.sh hands each value only to the service that needs it, at start
# time, so a secret exists in exactly one process.

# ── LLM provider ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Only for InvestPal's own backend agent (the /chat REST endpoint, the local web
# UI, backend-run workflows). The cockpit does not need a key: there,
# Claude Code is the LLM. Supply the one matching LLM_PROVIDER in .env.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# GOOGLE_API_KEY=

# ── Alpaca (stocks and ETFs) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Paper-trading keys by default; see ALPACA_API_BASE_URL in .env.
ALPACA_API_KEY=
ALPACA_API_SECRET=

# ── Coinbase (crypto) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Copy both straight out of the API key file Coinbase gives you: the "name"
# field into COINBASE_API_KEY, the "privateKey" field into COINBASE_API_SECRET.
# Paste privateKey exactly as it appears, on one line with its \n escapes intact.
# (Base64 of the PEM is also accepted, which is what older setups here used.)
COINBASE_API_KEY=
COINBASE_API_SECRET=

# ── Market data ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# OpenBB reaches 32 data providers, and most of what InvestPal asks for needs no
# credential: yfinance, SEC, ECB, IMF, OECD and the Federal Reserve are all
# keyless. Two keys are worth having. Both go here rather than in .env because
# OpenBB treats any variable whose name ends in API_KEY as a credential.
#
# Full provider-by-provider breakdown, and what each key buys: docs/market-data.md
#
# FRED — free, registration only, and in practice required rather than optional:
# commodity spot prices and most Federal Reserve series have no other free
# provider, so without it those tools return nothing at all.
# https://fredaccount.stlouisfed.org/apikeys
FRED_API_KEY=

# FMP — free tier is 250 requests/day. The single key that closes most of the
# gaps left by retiring the old server: financial ratios, worldwide news,
# revenue by segment and geography, analyst estimates, peer comparison,
# earnings-call transcripts and institutional ownership.
# https://site.financialmodelingprep.com/developer/docs
FMP_API_KEY=

# ── Turso Cloud sync ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Only needed when TURSO_SYNC_URL is set in .env.
TURSO_SYNC_AUTH_TOKEN=

# Interactive Brokers has no entry here on purpose: it authenticates through a
# browser login to its own gateway, never with an API key.
